 "summary": "Validates block index records and file metadata in BlockManager during node initialization. It rejects block index entries with missing or mismatched parent links and fails loading if the database reports a negative last-block-file number or an arbitrary file number lacking stored file info.",
 "problem": "Corrupted records in the LevelDB block index database can crash node initialization or cause undefined behavior. A negative last-block-file number causes an out-of-bounds vector read, while an entry with a null or height-mismatched parent pointer triggers an assertion failure in CBlockIndex::GetAncestor rather than failing cleanly with a reindex prompt.",
 "evidence": [
  "PR description and commit: \"A last block file number of -1 makes it read before the start of a vector. A very large one makes it allocate and read that many file infos. A block without a parent, or with a parent at the wrong height, hits the assert in CBlockIndex::GetAncestor.\"",
  "Unit tests in src/test/validation_chainstatemanager_tests.cpp inject corrupt database entries and verify LoadBlockIndex fails cleanly."
 ],
